From cce18c263e9623872327ba3c956012f73c1179cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Howells <dhowells@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 13:33:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] netfs: Fix missing locking around retry adding new subreqs

[ Upstream commit cce18c263e9623872327ba3c956012f73c1179cc ]

Fix netfs_retry_write_stream() to take the appropriate lock when
discarding excess subrequests from stream->subrequests and when
inserting newly allocated subrequests into stream->subrequests
during a write retry.

Without the lock, the write collection worker running concurrently
can walk stream->subrequests via list_next_entry() while these
unprotected list_del()/list_add() calls modify the list, causing
list corruption.

Also fix the 'to' cursor update: after inserting a new subreq with
list_add(&subreq->rreq_link, &to->rreq_link), 'to' must advance to
the newly inserted subreq (= subreq), not to the entry that was
already next in the list (list_next_entry(to, ...)).

Note: In 6.12.y write_retry.c does not exist yet; the equivalent
retry logic lives in write_collect.c::netfs_retry_write_stream().
The read retry path in read_retry.c already holds rreq->lock around
all modifications to rreq->subrequests and is not affected.

Fixes: 288ace2f57c9 ("netfs: New writeback implementation")
Closes: https://sashiko.dev/#/patchset/20260425125426.3855807-1-dhowells%40redhat.com
Signed-off-by: David Howells <dhowells@redhat.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260512123404.719402-3-dhowells@redhat.com
cc: Paulo Alcantara <pc@manguebit.org>
cc: netfs@lists.linux.dev
cc: linux-fsdevel@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Christian Brauner <brauner@kernel.org>
[Guru: write part of the code is not present in 6.12,
 hence not ported ]
Signed-off-by: Guruswamy Basavaiah <guruswamy.basavaiah@broadcom.com>
---
 fs/netfs/write_collect.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fs/netfs/write_collect.c b/fs/netfs/write_collect.c
--- a/fs/netfs/write_collect.c
+++ b/fs/netfs/write_collect.c
@@ -263,7 +263,9 @@
 			list_for_each_entry_safe_from(subreq, tmp,
 						      &stream->subrequests, rreq_link) {
 				trace_netfs_sreq(subreq, netfs_sreq_trace_discard);
+				spin_lock_bh(&wreq->lock);
 				list_del(&subreq->rreq_link);
+				spin_unlock_bh(&wreq->lock);
 				netfs_put_subrequest(subreq, false, netfs_sreq_trace_put_done);
 				if (subreq == to)
 					break;
@@ -287,8 +289,10 @@
 					     netfs_sreq_trace_new);
 			trace_netfs_sreq(subreq, netfs_sreq_trace_split);

+			spin_lock_bh(&wreq->lock);
 			list_add(&subreq->rreq_link, &to->rreq_link);
-			to = list_next_entry(to, rreq_link);
+			spin_unlock_bh(&wreq->lock);
+			to = subreq;
 			trace_netfs_sreq(subreq, netfs_sreq_trace_retry);

 			stream->sreq_max_len	= len;
--
